# Task 4 calibration renders (~180 MB of WAVs, regenerated by tools/calibrate
# + tools/analyze_calibration.py) -- but calib/calibration.json itself is
# small (~2 KB) and IS committed, via an explicit `git add -f`.
calib/

# No Roland PCM ships here -- no samples, no patch data.
#
# The impulse responses DO ship. They are the JV reverb's response to a
# synthetic impulse WE generate and inject into a copy of the wave ROM, so no
# Roland waveform is present in the signal: the same thing as an IR pack of a
# hardware reverb. Shipping them means a user gets working presets without
# running the calibrate stage at all.
#
# calib/ir/ is the superseded deconvolution bank, kept out as dead weight.
calib/ir/
calib/ds_probe/
calib/ds_state.bin
docs/superpowers/
